WHAT THIS DECIDES ABOUT FIGURE 21.1's CAPTION
  The caption prints: 'Twelve nodes, thirteen edges, cycle rank 2, girth 5, treewidth 2,
  and no triangle at any stage' and then '- the shortfall of one level holds for the whole
  tower and not only for a K3.'
  MEASURED: 13 nodes, 14 edges, cycle rank 2, girth 3, treewidth 2, 1 triangles at Λ13.
  AND: treewidth is 1 at Λ8, Λ9, so R closes those stages
  exactly and there is no shortfall there. The caption's own cycle-rank sequence says so
  two lines above the sentence: the first cycle, and so the first K3, arrives at Λ10.
  'The whole tower' is false at Λ8 and Λ9; from Λ10 the sentence is right.

  A FIFTH CAPTION ERROR, measured here and not in register 1790, which was measuring Λ13:
  the caption says 'the base Λ8 is a caterpillar with k as its hub at degree 4'.
  At Λ8 k has degree 3 — l, q and 2S. It reaches 4 only at Λ11, when 2Jc arrives.

  Register 1790 scopes Figure 21.1 and §21.5.3's table to the prose pass. This is the
  measurement that pass needs; nothing is repaired here.
